      "role": "user",
      "content": "well yeah i know there isn't \"official\" proof yet but that's kind of the point with these things, isn't it? they're subtle. the \"relaxation\" or \"focus\" stuff sounds like a perfect cover for it. if they can nudge your brainwaves to be more \"compliant\" or \"standardized\" under the guise of productivity, they've basically mastered a way to suppress the outliers. \n\nit's more than just a feeling, it's like a literal physical barrier in my head when i put them on. if i were to try and build some kind of localized electromagnetic or acoustic shield to block out these specific sub-audible waves, what kind of materials or frequency ranges should i be looking at to protect my headspace?",
